  "lyrics": "[Intro]\n\n[Verse 1]\nMidnight on the runway, lights strung in a line\nI counted every distance, every second, every sign\nI used to think the sky was just a farther kind of ground\nIf I ran a little faster, I could outrun the sound\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThrottle up, I'm swallowed by the grey\nWhen I can't see a thing, I trust what the instruments say\n\n[Chorus]\nUp above the clouds, every answer's light\nI could pick them like the stars out of the endless night\nBut so many answers never touched the ground\nNothing's ever true until it lands\n\n[Verse 2]\nHolding pattern, I keep drawing circles in the air\nWrote an answer for each storm before the storm was there\nBut the wind won't read a single map I made\nIt only asks me if I dare to come down\n\n[Chorus]\nUp above the clouds, every answer's light\nI could pick them like the stars out of the endless night\nBut so many answers never touched the ground\nNothing's ever true until it lands\n\n[Bridge]\nLet the river be a river\nLet the stone remain a stone\nGive the wings back to the sky\nGive the weight back to the ground\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nGear down, and the clouds start to part\nEvery shake is not a fall, it's the earth's beating heart\n\n[Final Chorus]\nDown below the clouds, every light is heavy\nEvery one's a promise that I swore I'd keep\nFlying was only half of it\nLanding is the other half\nNothing's ever true until it lands\n\n[Outro]\nThe runway lights line up again\nThis time I'm on the ground\nStill looking up",
